   "text": "Same as random on 1h and 4h. Worse than random on daily, but that is fragile: it rests on one stretch of SOL signals."
  }
 ],
 "notes": [
  "On 1h, %K crossing up through %D below 20 gave 6,623 entries in 3,165 separate moves. After 20 candles they were 0.01% ahead of random entries, inside the luck band of -0.08% to 0.1%. Holding %K below 20 enters about six times as often and lands at 0. The extra entries are repeats of the same dips, not new information.",
  "On daily, the short on %K crossing down through %D above 80 did 3.2% worse than random after 20 days. It was also worse at 10 and 50 days, but not at 100. It disappears once the signals between Jul 27 and Aug 21, 2021 are left out. SOL carried it at 9% worse than random, while BTC was 1.21% ahead, inside its band.",
  "The same daily short splits by regime. In uptrends it did 5.4% worse than random, resting on the same stretch of signals. In downtrends it was 0.93% worse, inside the luck band. Price kept rising after these crosses only while the pair traded above its 200-day SMA.",
  "On 4h, dip entries in downtrends looked worse than random: 0.39% for %K below 20 and 0.42% for the %K cross up through %D below 20. Both disappear without the signals on Nov 6–14, 2022 and Nov 7–10, 2022, during the FTX collapse. Both were worse at 10 candles and the same as random at 50 and 100. In uptrends both were the same as random.",
  "Single SOL stretches produced the other daily results. The %K cross up through %D below 20 did 6.17% worse than random on SOL, resting on 6 entries between Apr 12 and May 14, 2022. %K above 80 as a short did 4.79% worse on SOL, resting on 46 entries between May 18 and Sep 9, 2021. Neither shows on BTC or ETH.",
  "For a long DCA bot on these pairs, StochRSI oversold timing did not change what price did next. The DCA orders and take profit carry the result. If you keep StochRSI, use it as a filter beside a trend condition, because its worst dip entries came in downtrend crashes. For a short bot, the daily overbought crosses ran into uptrends that kept going, which is a reason to leave them out."
